Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ava integrates with and can bundle third-party software and models that carry
their OWN licenses, which apply to those components. Notable examples:

  - Agent runtime: NVIDIA NemoClaw / OpenClaw (Apache-2.0,
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/NemoClaw), run in an NVIDIA OpenShell sandbox.
    Installed on demand by NVIDIA's official installer (the npm package is a
    stub) and not redistributed in this repository; upstream is an alpha
    project.
  - Inference engines (e.g. vLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp) — their respective licenses.
  - Models / checkpoints you download (LLMs) — each has its own license and
    acceptable-use terms. Review before use.
  - Weather data: Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com), used by the built-in
    `get_weather` tool. The data is licensed CC BY 4.0 and the free API tier is
    non-commercial only; commercial deployments need an Open-Meteo
    subscription.
  - Python dependencies — see requirements*.txt; Node dependencies for the web
    app — see frontend/package.json — and their upstream licenses.

Ava does not display model license terms during install. Before you pull a
model, read its license: the Llama-family defaults are under Meta's Llama
Community License. Provisioning the agent runtime runs NVIDIA's installer with
NEMOCLAW_ACCEPT_THIRD_PARTY_SOFTWARE=1, which accepts NemoClaw's third-party
software terms on your behalf. It is the operator's responsibility to comply
with the terms of any model or component they choose to install.
